# `held` is a Map or a Set. Link keeps the set of the classes, so a read or a call by name is looked up on each of them; before, two classes in one value were "some classes", the read was a read of a name off what nobody knows, and the call a call of it.
# RUN: link lookups mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: lookup name-read "size"
# CHECK-NOT: lookup name-called "clear"
# CHECK: lookup read MapPrototypeSize
# CHECK: lookup read SetPrototypeSize
# CHECK: lookup called MapPrototypeClear
# CHECK: lookup called SetPrototypeClear
# Both getters answer an integer.
# RUN(RESULT): link functions mechanisms=all
# RESULT: function f1 {{*}}result=i32
